Notes on this run
 - The four console lines are the answers that this script asks for on purpose: a second POST for the same player (409), the
   evidence "javascript:alert(1)" sent straight to the API (400), the page sending an appeal after the server had closed the window
   under it (403, shown to the user as "The appeal window is closed"), and a direct API call after the deadline (403). The page itself
   produced no error, warning or failed request of its own.
 - A first run of this script showed a 404 in the console on EVERY visit to a dossier: the page asks "has an appeal been filed?"
   and the API answered 404 for "no". The API now answers 200 with null (see AI_FAILURE_AUDIT, entry #06).
 - Section 3 changes what the page believes about the device clock (Date.now is shifted by one hour); it does not change the
   operating system clock. Section 4 blocks the main thread of the page for 3 seconds. Section 5 uses a second tab to hide the first.
